      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "[codex] acknowledge terminal Gmail OAuth watch failures",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- classify expired or revoked Gmail OAuth credentials as terminal processing failures\n- acknowledge terminal OAuth failures in both Pub/Sub push and pull consumers\n- preserve the last successfully processed Gmail history cursor for later catch-up\n- keep transient Gmail API, rate-limit, and downstream hook failures retryable\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe Gmail watch consumers treated every non-rate-limit processing failure as retryable. When the OAuth refresh token returned `invalid_grant`, push delivery responded with HTTP 500 and pull delivery nacked the message. Pub/Sub then redelivered a failure that cannot recover without operator re-authentication, producing an unbounded retry and log storm.\n\n## User impact\n\nExpired or revoked Gmail credentials now produce a clear re-authentication warning and acknowledge the current Pub/Sub notification without advancing the stored history cursor. A later notification after re-authentication can resume from the last successfully processed history ID. Temporary API failures and hook delivery failures retain their existing retry behavior.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `go test ./internal/gmailwatch -run 'Test(HTTPHandlerAcknowledgesTerminalAuthFailure|ProcessorClassifiesTerminalAuthWithoutAdvancingHistory)$'`\n- `go test ./internal/cmd -run 'Test(IsTerminalGmailAuthError|GmailWatchPullMessage_AcksTerminalAuthAndPreservesProgress|GmailWatchServer_AcknowledgesTerminalAuthAndPreservesProgress)$'`\n- `make fmt-check`\n- `make lint`\n- `make deadcode`\n- `make build`\n\nThe broader `internal/cmd` Gmail-watch test selection still has pre-existing shared-state failures when run as one package on this machine. The same failures reproduce on unmodified `upstream/main`; the focused regression tests above pass.\n\nRelated OpenClaw lifecycle fix: openclaw/openclaw#96202.\n",
        "branch": "codex/gmail-oauth-terminal-ack",
        "head_sha": "554028d36b9c05bae292c22eb91c0201adcea5cb",
        "author": "litang9",
